> What are other ways to say "a sister report"-- like another report co-produced with this one?
**assistant**:
> Here are some alternatives you can use to refer to "a sister report" that emphasize the aspect of co-production or collaboration:
> 
> 1. **Companion Report** - This suggests that the reports are meant to go together or complement each other.
> 2. **Partner Report** - This highlights the collaborative nature of the reports.
> 3. **Collaborative Report** - Emphasizes the joint effort in production.
> 4. **Concomitant Report** - Indicates that the reports are naturally associated or occur together.
> 5. **Coordinated Report** - Suggests that the reports were produced with mutual consideration and aligned objectives.
> 6. **Parallel Report** - Implies that the reports were developed side by side with shared or related goals.
> 7. **Joint Report** - Stresses a combined or united effort in creating the reports.
> 
> Each of these options can convey slightly different nuances, so the best choice may depend on the specific context and focus you want to emphasize.
